CFI.co Governance — Step 2 agreement of a principal

I, Marten Mark, one of the three principals named in CFI.co's Business Continuity and
Governance Authority Instrument, agree to the adoption of the CFI.co governance file as
Public Edition v1.0 (internal v3.0).

The version I agree to is the file governance-public-edition-v1.0.docx, whose SHA-256 is:

    6829072874467AB111D4A68C3A1D36FF111E5ACA52501B2EB13E287130B567CB

That is the adopted text. A UTF-8 export of it is published alongside for reading by people
and machines; the export is a rendering of this file and not a second version of it.

My agreement is given under Step 2 of the adoption block, which requires the director of
Magnus Publications Ltd together with at least one other principal. Anthony Michael enters my
name and the date on my behalf, at my written instruction of 1 August 2026. This statement is
that instruction in a form a third party can verify without having to trust either of us.

My agreement was given on two conditions, and they are part of it rather than context to it:
that no row of the commencement schedule is signed with a blank deadline, and that the
requirement for a passing evaluation run is resolved openly rather than passed over in
silence. Both were met before this was signed. Every deadline cell in the schedule carries a
date; the blanks that remain are in the Commenced column, which cannot be completed inside a
file at the moment that file is hashed. The evaluation requirement was amended before
adoption so that it governs use rather than adoption, and the file states in its operative
text that the run had not taken place when it was adopted.

What this signature proves, stated so that no one reads more into it than it carries: it
proves that the holder of the key below produced this text. It does not by itself prove that
two people independently exercised judgement, and it is not offered as proof of that. It is
offered as the one part of the adoption record a reader can check without taking our word for
anything.

The key is held by me personally, on a machine CFI.co does not operate. Its fingerprint is
published at _principal-mark.cfi.co and on keys.openpgp.org.

    C5FD 9221 0CCF 0D31 271E  A4BC 6B68 1CAA A8BA A1FE

Marten Mark
1 August 2026
